<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Limitations</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although Orchestra-o1 achieves strong omnimodal agentic intelligence, several limitations remain.
First, orchestration introduces additional system complexity. Compared with a single native omnimodal agent, Orchestra-o1 requires maintaining sub-agent histories, tool schemas, backend configurations, cost accounting, and asynchronous execution. While this design improves modularity and efficiency, it also creates more implementation components that must be carefully engineered and monitored.
Second, the current training recipe focuses on the main agent rather than jointly optimizing all sub-agents and tools. DA-GRPO improves decision-level orchestration, but the sub-agent backends remain fixed during training. A more complete learning system could jointly adapt the main agent, sub-agent policies, and tool-selection behavior from end-to-end task outcomes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"></p>
</div>
</section>
